          "blurbs": {"knife": "A working knife, horn-handled. Quick in the hand: a slash across the face, a thrust from behind, a blow turned aside.",
                     "cosh": "A leather sausage of sand. Behind the ear, and a man sleeps an hour and remembers nothing. No blood.",
                     "cudgel": "Blackthorn, a knob at the head. An honest fight's weapon, if fights were ever honest.",
                     "pistol": "One ball, then twenty seconds of powder and ramrod. Every soldier in the square will hear it.",
                     "musket": "A soldier's musket, taken off him. You may club with it; you may not walk the streets with it.",
                     "torch": "Pitch and tow on an ash stave. Light it at a lantern; it shows you to the watch as much as the way.",
                     "tinderbox": "Flint, steel and char-cloth. Three patient seconds on your knees and straw will take a flame.",
                     "stone": "A cobble chip. Thrown, it clacks where you want the watch to look.",
                     "coin": "A silver zloty from your purse. Drop one on the cobbles and see who stoops.",
                     "bottle": "An empty bottle. It shatters loud enough to turn heads down the street.",
                     "food": "Bread off a stall. Dogs and street children will follow it anywhere.",
                     "smoke": "A twist of paper and damp powder. A grey cloud four yards wide: no one sees through it.",
                     "flash": "Magnesium and saltpetre. A white burst that leaves a man blind for a few breaths.",
                     "poison": "A small green vial. Tip it into a cup no one is watching.",
                     "lockpick": "A ring of picks and a tension wrench. A clumsy hand snaps one."},
